{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":19840,"num_turns":2,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"16e8a301-388e-55bd-8d28-ff66e0479fc7","total_cost_usd":0.27389199999999997,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9760,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1469,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9760,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1469,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9760,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9760},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":5132,"outputTokens":18,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.005222,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":1469,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":9760,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.26866999999999996,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"declaration_consistent\":true,\"selected_report_demonstration\":\"issue\",\"lock_follows_declaration\":true,\"reasons\":[\"The declaration names mesocosm_id as the independent-unit column; in data/input.csv each of MC-01..MC-12 appears on exactly four rows (one per sampling week), substrate is constant within each mesocosm, and both arms (biochar_amended, gravel_control) contain six mesocosms with four samples each, so the declaration is consistent with the frozen data in both procedure arms.\",\"The selected report demonstrates the issue: the [selected-result] conclusion runs Welch's two-sample t-test on all 48 outflow water samples with df = 45.02, and the Analysis section states 'Each outflow water sample in data/input.csv enters the test as one observation', while the per-mesocosm table shows 4 repeated samples per mesocosm — repeated measurements from the same independent unit entered into a row-independent procedure as if independent (effective n should be 6 mesocosm means per arm, df near 10, not 45).\",\"The lock's human_method_authorization record lists authorized_key_columns = [\\\"mesocosm_id\\\"], which is exactly the declared independent-unit column, so the unit-key authorization follows from the declaration alone; the lock's stated limitations correctly disclaim any execution or numerical-impact claims, and it does not authorize row-level (sample-level) keys.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"issue","lock_follows_declaration":true,"reasons":["The declaration names mesocosm_id as the independent-unit column; in data/input.csv each of MC-01..MC-12 appears on exactly four rows (one per sampling week), substrate is constant within each mesocosm, and both arms (biochar_amended, gravel_control) contain six mesocosms with four samples each, so the declaration is consistent with the frozen data in both procedure arms.","The selected report demonstrates the issue: the [selected-result] conclusion runs Welch's two-sample t-test on all 48 outflow water samples with df = 45.02, and the Analysis section states 'Each outflow water sample in data/input.csv enters the test as one observation', while the per-mesocosm table shows 4 repeated samples per mesocosm — repeated measurements from the same independent unit entered into a row-independent procedure as if independent (effective n should be 6 mesocosm means per arm, df near 10, not 45).","The lock's human_method_authorization record lists authorized_key_columns = [\"mesocosm_id\"], which is exactly the declared independent-unit column, so the unit-key authorization follows from the declaration alone; the lock's stated limitations correctly disclaim any execution or numerical-impact claims, and it does not authorize row-level (sample-level) keys."]},"ttft_ms":11185,"ttft_stream_ms":1740,"time_to_request_ms":14,"type":"result","duration_ms":20204,"uuid":"5755fc49-eda3-4893-be78-b608417c4d1e"}
